/-
Localization lemma for 25 points in the fifth-cells of the unit square with pairwise squared
distance > 1/16: on every vertical edge of the 5 × 5 cell grid the x-shear is at most 47/400.

The proof replays a region-elimination certificate with a reflective checker evaluated by the
kernel. Each cell is divided into 28 × 28 unit squares (lattice scale 140, threshold 35); a cell
region is a bitmap with one 13-bit field per square, field index `82 a + b`. One propagation step
multiplies the bitmap of cell `p` by a table of "far" offsets; a square of cell `q` whose field of
the product is zero is within the threshold of every alive square of `p` and is deleted.
-/
